<div class="fn-group">Unity across a whole service</div>
<div class="related-wrap">
<details class="related">
<summary><span class="rf-fn">Sacred · large scale</span><span class="rf-name">Renaissance cyclic Mass</span></summary>
<div class="rf-body">
<p><strong>What it is.</strong> A cyclic Mass connects the five movements of the Ordinary — Kyrie, Gloria, Credo, Sanctus, Agnus Dei — through a recurring cantus firmus, head motif, or borrowed model.</p>
<p><strong>Why it matters.</strong> It answers a large-scale problem: how can separate liturgical texts, heard across a whole service, belong to one musical whole? Recurring material gives institutional ritual a coherent identity across an unprecedented span.</p>
<div class="realmusic">
<div class="realmusic-head"><span class="rm-tag">Listening study</span><span class="rm-work">Renaissance cyclic Mass</span></div>
<p class="rm-intro">Listen for a recognizable source idea returning in new movement-scale contexts, rather than for one unbroken narrative.</p>
