<div class="fn-group">The same craft, turned toward words</div>
<div class="related-wrap">
<details class="related">
<summary><span class="rf-fn">Secular · vernacular</span><span class="rf-name">Through-composed madrigal</span></summary>
<div class="rf-body">
<p><strong>What it is.</strong> The madrigal is a secular vocal form for a small ensemble. In a through-composed setting, new music answers each new image or rhetorical turn of the poem rather than repeating one tune per stanza.</p>
<p><strong>Why it matters.</strong> It embodies Renaissance humanism — individual words deserve exact musical response. Word-painting and abrupt expressive changes widen the period well beyond a serene sacred sound-world. <strong>Hear it as the second reading in the hero player above:</strong> notice how a textual turn changes texture, pace, or register instead of returning to a fixed refrain.</p>
</div>
</details>
