<section class="chapter" id="enlightenment" style="--acc:#698BA1;--acc-soft:color-mix(in oklab,#698BA1 15%,white)">
<div class="chapter-head">
<span class="chapter-sig" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40"><rect x="7" y="12" width="26" height="18"></rect><line x1="7" y1="21" x2="33" y2="21"></line><line x1="20" y1="12" x2="20" y2="30"></line></svg></span>
<div><div class="chapter-eyebrow">Period 04 · The Enlightenment · Classical style</div><h2 class="chapter-title">Enlightenment</h2></div>
<p class="chapter-claim">Classical form as public, intelligible architecture — balanced phrases, clear cadences, and satisfying returns let complexity work beneath a transparent surface.</p>
</div>
<p class="hero-marker">Hero form · Sonata form</p>
<p class="body">Sonata form moves through exposition, development, and recapitulation. Contrasting thematic areas are presented in different keys, destabilized and recombined in the development section, then finally returned in a home-key reconciliation. Where a fugue works one idea continuously, sonata form <em>stages a conflict and then settles it</em>: it needs two identities and two key areas so that their eventual agreement can mean something.</p>
<p class="body">This changes the role of the audience. Sonata form asks you to <strong>remember multiple thematic ideas across long spans and unconsciously feel the tension of journeying from the “home” of the first theme</strong> — to notice you have been taken somewhere, held in instability, and brought back. Its pleasures are narrative and public: departure, suspense, recognition, closure. That is precisely why it suited the Enlightenment's new paying concert audience, who could follow a dramatic argument without any training in counterpoint.</p>
<div class="realmusic">
<div class="realmusic-head"><span class="rm-tag">Hero study</span><span class="rm-work">Compact sonata form</span></div>
<p class="rm-intro">Remember the two opening identities; notice how the development fragments them, and how the recapitulation changes the <em>meaning</em> of their return by bringing both into the home key. The lower lane traces the tonal journey — how far from home you are at any moment.</p>
