<div class="rf-body">
<p><strong>What it is.</strong> A symphony or large chamber work commonly unfolds as fast opening, slow movement, minuet/trio (later scherzo), and fast finale — each with its own internal form.</p>
<p><strong>Why it matters.</strong> The cycle creates architecture at two scales at once: local movement design and a long-range journey through tempos, keys, and characters. It became the principal framework for public instrumental music — and the structure Romantic composers would enlarge.</p>
