<div class="fn-group">An inherited frame, new energy</div>
<div class="related-wrap">
<details class="related">
<summary><span class="rf-fn">Transition form</span><span class="rf-name">Scherzo &amp; trio</span></summary>
<div class="rf-body">
<p><strong>What it is.</strong> The scherzo inherits the minuet-and-trio ABA frame but accelerates it, sharpens the contrast, and often disrupts phrase or accent. Beethoven established it as a symphonic alternative to the minuet.</p>
<p><strong>Why it matters.</strong> It is the ideal transition form: Classical architecture stays audible while Romantic energy changes its bodily character from courtly balance to speed, surprise, force, or the uncanny.</p>
<div class="realmusic">
<div class="realmusic-head"><span class="rm-tag">Listening study</span><span class="rm-work">Scherzo &amp; trio</span></div>
<p class="rm-intro">Compare its returning outer frame with the Classical minuet, then notice how speed, accent, and character make the inherited form feel newly unstable.</p>
