  <p class="clip-title"><strong>Twelve-tone organization</strong><span>one ordered row · four basic transformations · layered conclusion</span></p>
  <p class="sr-only">A twelve-note row supplies every section. Prime, inversion, retrograde, and retrograde inversion preserve the ordered pitch-class relationships by transposing, mirroring, reversing, or combining those operations.</p>

